# Cloudflare Worker runtime bindings/vars for local `vinext dev` — this is
# Wrangler's own convention (a `.dev.vars` file at the project root), separate
# from Next.js's `.env.local` (see .env.example). Copy this file to
# `.dev.vars` and fill in real values; `.dev.vars` itself is gitignored and
# must never be committed.
#
# For production, set these via `wrangler secret put <NAME>` (secrets) or the
# Cloudflare dashboard — not via a committed file either way.
#
# The `DB` (D1) binding is intentionally NOT listed here: it comes from
# `.openai/hosting.json`'s `d1` field (see vite.config.ts), not from
# .dev.vars/env vars. As of 2026-08-07 it is unprovisioned (`"d1": null`) —
# see .solo/risks.md and .solo/prd.md Open Question #5.

# Optional. POST target for the fire-and-forget error webhook in
# worker/index.ts (e.g. a Slack/Discord incoming webhook, or a monitoring
# provider's ingest URL). If unset, errors still log via console.error /
# `wrangler tail` — this only adds an external notification on top. See
# .solo/monitoring.md.
MONITORING_WEBHOOK_URL=
